  "order": 1,
  "summary": "Say hello, goodbye, and introduce yourself.",
  "focus": "Fixed greeting expressions and 'me llamo'",
  "content": "## Saying hello\n\n- **Hola**: hi / hello (any time of day)\n- **Buenos días**: good morning (until lunch)\n- **Buenas tardes**: good afternoon / early evening\n- **Buenas noches**: good evening / good night\n\n## Asking how someone is\n\n- **¿Qué tal?**: how's it going? (informal, very common)\n- **¿Cómo estás?**: how are you? (informal, *tú*)\n- **¿Cómo está usted?**: how are you? (formal)\n- **Bien, gracias. ¿Y tú?**: fine, thanks. And you?\n\n## Introducing yourself\n\n- **Me llamo Ana.**: My name is Ana. (literally *I call myself Ana*)\n- **Soy Ana.**: I'm Ana.\n- **¿Cómo te llamas?**: What's your name? (informal)\n- **¿Cómo se llama usted?**: What's your name? (formal)\n- **Mucho gusto.** / **Encantado.** (said by a man) / **Encantada.** (said by a woman): nice to meet you.\n\n## Saying goodbye\n\n- **Adiós**: goodbye\n- **Hasta luego**: see you later\n- **Hasta mañana**: see you tomorrow\n- **Nos vemos**: see you\n\n> Remember the upside-down marks: questions start with **¿** and exclamations with **¡**.",
